      "writtenOn": "2020-09-23T19:14:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Most compat_ioctl() implementations return -ENOIOCTLCMD.\n\nIt seems the reason for doing that is now obsolete, though, so I suppose we should just use ENOTTY for both.\n\n(ENOIOCTLCMD enabled fallback to the ioctl translation table defined in fs/compat_ioctl.c.  But that was removed in Linux v5.6, and this driver isn\u0027t using that table anyway.)",
      "parentUuid": "edd55f3e_d8d00d3d",
      "revId": "a931a7e6579fe51b38214b5feec390fc5d4cea0b",
